																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13886756/scp-idea:the-answer-sheet">SCP Idea: &quot;The Answer Sheet&quot;</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4830903">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong></p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Regular SCP layout</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A regular looking piece of paper and an ink pen, that when written on using the aforementioned pen, grants a reply from the paper. The entity that replies through the paper is hyperintelligent, having knowledge of the O5 council and Level 5 clearance information that's withheld even from the researchers working on the SCP. It also has the ability to force anyone to grant any request that they read, which leads to many attempted escapes.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> A pair of entities, a pen and piece of paper, is discovered within an undisclosed SCP Site storage closet. After a junior researcher attempts to use the pen and paper together, he turns it in to his higher-ups, who begin experimentation on the entity. After discovering it's many abilities, such as it's incredible knowledge and it's way of making peopel complete requests, it is given strict safety and testing measures.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The way that the paper is very knowledagble about the Foundation, and how it can make people grant it's requests. It's a mysterious entity that much isn't known about, which leads to myriad tests on said entity.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> Looking especially for critique on how it makes people fufill the requests of readers, or if there's something that could work better with the idea.</p>

							</div>

								
					
